{
  "about": [
    "The real cars: one entry per car, read by tools/prepare-cars.mjs (which makes the game files from",
    "  skip: why a car is left out (it isn't built or shown in the game)",
    "  held: why a car is held back for now (it stays out of the game, the credits and the generated lists).",
    "        `node tools/prepare-cars.mjs --hold` moves the held cars' built files (and their vehicles.json",
    "        rows) to tools/.cache/cars/held; `node tools/prepare-cars.mjs --unhold <id,id|all>` clears the",
    "        mark, moves the files back and writes src/realCars.json and CREDITS.md again. Then check the car",
    "        in the game (tools/check-cars.js) before uploading.",
    "the Sketchfab downloads in tools/.cache/sketchfab/cars) and, through src/realCars.json, by the game.",
    "A car whose file isn't downloaded yet is skipped, so entries can be added before the files arrive.",
    "  file: the GLB, relative to tools/.cache/sketchfab/cars",
    "  length, width, wheelbase: the real car's, in metres (length sets the scale; the others are checked)",
    "  flip: true when the model's nose points the other way. Check it by eye with --preview (the yellow",
    "        headlights belong at the right in the side view) and in the game; left out, the script guesses",
    "        from where the red lamps are",
    "  yaw: optional extra turn in degrees, for a model that isn't lined up with its own axes",
    "  kw, kg, topKmh, zeroTo100 (seconds), drive (RWD/FWD/AWD): the real car's figures; the game's",
    "        handling is worked out from them (src/garage.js). grip and redline are optional; a car that",
    "        can't reach 100 km/h gives zeroTo80 instead of zeroTo100.",
    "  sound: everyday (four cylinders), sports (six or more), diesel or electric; electric: true for EVs",
    "  traffic: true for everyday cars that may drive around in traffic on High",
    "  parts: optional fixes when the names in a model don't say what a part is. Each is a regular",
    "        expression matched against 'node name|mesh name|material name|#material number'",
    "        (see them with --parts): drop, body, lamp, glass, interior, caliper; tail adds parts whose",
    "        red areas are brake lamps without making them glow at night; brake names brake lamps of any colour",
    "  colours: optional { regular expression: \"#rrggbb\" } to repaint parts (a placeholder paint, say)",
    "  keep: optional box (in the model's own units) outside which everything is dropped",
    "  maxHeight: optional height in metres above which every triangle is cut away (an aerial joined to the roof)",
    "  credit: the Sketchfab page it came from (CC BY 4.0 unless license says otherwise); original:",
    "        the first upload, when the file says it is a copy of someone else's model"
  ],
